# Build context trim for `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` (root context, whole reactor).
#
# docker/Dockerfile deliberately does `COPY . .` rather than listing modules: `service` depends on
# `qits-stt-domain`, a 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT this repo never publishes, so its sources have to be in the
# context — and a module list would have to be edited every time a module is added. This file is
# what makes that cheap: it drops everything the build does not read, so adding a module stays free
# and no stale output leaks in.

.git
.gitignore

# Maven / Quarkus build output — regenerated inside the build stage, and ~84 MB of it here (the
# native binary and the fast-jar dominate). Copying it in would also risk a stale target/ shadowing
# what the stage compiles.
**/target
**/target-ide

# Local env / IDE cruft. `.sdkmanrc` in particular would be actively misleading in the context: it
# names the GraalVM a developer uses, and the build stage brings its own native-image.
.env
.idea
.vscode
.settings
*.iml
.sdkmanrc

# Home-relative caches a tool leaks into the repo root when run with the repo as its cwd (they are
# in .gitignore for the same reason). `.m2` can be gigabytes, and the build stage populates its own.
.cache
.m2
.local

# Docs — including the generated docs/openapi.yml — and the docker/ dir itself: nothing in the build
# reads them, and keeping them out means editing this Dockerfile or a README does not bust the
# `COPY . .` layer and force a fresh native compile.
*.md
docs
docker
